  "content": {
    "id": "p10-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Simplify. In this question, $a$, $b$ and $c$ are positive and not equal to $1$.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p10-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$(\\log_a b)(\\log_b a)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(\\log_a b)(\\log_b a)&=\\frac{\\log_{10}b}{\\log_{10}a}\\times\\frac{\\log_{10}a}{\\log_{10}b}\\\\(\\log_a b)(\\log_b a)&=1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p10-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$(\\log_a b)(\\log_b c)(\\log_c a)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$1$",
          "worked": "By the change-of-base product formula, $(\\log_a b)(\\log_b c)=\\log_a c$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(\\log_a b)(\\log_b c)(\\log_c a)&=(\\log_a c)(\\log_c a)\\\\(\\log_a b)(\\log_b c)(\\log_c a)&=\\frac{\\log_a c}{\\log_a c}\\\\(\\log_a b)(\\log_b c)(\\log_c a)&=1\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
  },
